# Frontend Rules

## Required Reading

Before modifying frontend code, read:
- `docs/architecture/frontend.md` — component hierarchy and state management
- `docs/file-structure.md` — folder conventions
- `frontend/lib/core/queryKeys.ts` — existing query key patterns
- `frontend/lib/core/invalidation.ts` — cache invalidation patterns

## Pages (app/ Router)

1. Pages are thin shells. They wire one primary hook and render one primary component.

2. Always add `"use client"` if the page uses hooks, state, or browser APIs. Otherwise omit.

3. Route files live in `app/{path}/page.tsx`. Admin pages under `app/marketplace/admin/`.

## Components

4. One component per file. File name matches export name exactly.

5. Domain prefix for scoped components: `Marketplace*`, `Collection*`, `RwaDetail*`, `Portfolio*`.

6. Shared UI in `components/ui/`. Domain components in `components/{domain}/`.

7. Admin components in `components/marketplace/admin/`. Export from `components/marketplace/admin/index.ts`.

8. Components only render UI and delegate all data fetching/mutation to hooks.

## Hooks

9. Every data-fetching concern gets a dedicated hook in `hooks/{domain}/`.

10. Naming: `use{FeatureName}.ts`. Always `"use client"` at top.

11. Use React Query for server state. Use Zustand stores only for global client state.

12. Always provide `queryKey` from `queryKeys.ts` for all `useQuery` calls.

13. Add a new key to `queryKeys.ts` for every new data entity fetched.

14. Add cache invalidation in `lib/core/invalidation.ts` for mutations that affect cached data.

15. State machine pattern for forms: `type Step = 'idle' | 'pending' | 'success' | 'error'`.

16. Use `submitLockRef` to prevent double-submit on async operations.

## API Clients

17. API client functions in `lib/core/api/{domain}.ts` — one file per backend module.

18. Functions return typed results. Do not use `any`.

19. Use `apiFetch` (or `fetch` with base URL from env) — never hard-code API hostnames.

## State Management

20. `useAuthStore` — user session, login/logout. Do not put marketplace data here.

21. `useAuthUiStore` — modal state only (sign-in, wallet connect, KYC, returnTo).

22. `useAppStore` — wallet address, USDC balance, refreshTick.

23. React Query owns all server-fetched data. Do not store API responses in Zustand.

## Authentication / Access Gates

24. Use `useTradeAccessGate()` before any trade action (requires linked wallet).

25. Use `useSellAccessGate()` before vault/sell actions (requires KYC approved).

26. Never bypass access gates. They open the appropriate modal for the user.

27. Use `useEnsureAccountWalletReady()` before signing any transaction — it ensures the Privy embedded wallet is initialized.

## Seaport & Blockchain

28. Seaport typed data must be signed via `useSeaportOrderSigner` — which prefers Privy embedded wallet.

29. For USDC approvals: use `useERC20ApproveIfNeeded` from wagmi hooks.

30. The `x-tokenable-chain-id` header is set by `setActiveChainIdForApi()` and read by the backend's `ChainConfigService`.

31. Do not call `TokenableRWA.mint()` or `adminBurn()` from frontend. Those are backend-only.

## Constants

32. Contract addresses come from `constants/contracts.ts` (derived from `NEXT_PUBLIC_CHAIN_*` env vars).

33. `NEXT_PUBLIC_*` env vars are baked at build time — changing them requires a frontend rebuild.

## TypeScript

34. No `any` types in new code. Use `unknown` with type narrowing if needed.

35. React Query returns typed data — define the response type in `lib/core/api/` files.

36. Run `pnpm exec tsc --noEmit` before considering a change complete.
